    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Which factor(s) determine whether the exponential graph approaches the horizontal asymptote $y=h$ from above or below?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Only the sign of $k$: from above if $k>0$ and from below if $k<0$.",
      "worked": "The exponential factor is always positive.\n$$y-h=k(a^{\\pm x})$$\nThus $y-h$ has the sign of $k$. If $k>0$, the graph lies above $y=h$ and approaches it from above. If $k<0$, the graph lies below $y=h$ and approaches it from below.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
